<h3>Knowledge Generation Trigger — Only Changes Accepted as Done</h3>
<p>Not every Commit is turned into knowledge immediately. During development, unfinished implementations, failed attempts, and temporary fixes are all mixed in. Only what passes the gate the organization accepts as done &mdash; <strong>a change that has gone through Review, been Merged into a baseline Branch, and whose Pipeline succeeded</strong> &mdash; becomes a target for analysis. Deciding what inside a completed change is knowledge and what is not (the criteria that exclude mechanical Refactoring, typos, and the like) is handled by the value assessment in <a href="#!dzp-knowledge">the knowledge management system</a>.</p>

